// trianglebench-cpu - the same triangle-counting problem as trianglebench, solved on the CPU only.
//
//   triangles(G) = trace(A^3) / 6 = sum_ij A_ij * (A*A)_ij / 6        (A = 0/1 adjacency matrix)
//
//   C1  CPU cores, INT64 : own OpenMP kernel, rows as 64-bit bitsets, (A*A)_ij = popcount(row_i AND row_j)
//                          (identical work to GPU method M1: all n^2 pairs, mask applied afterwards)
//   C2  CPU cores, FP32  : BLAS sgemm C = A*A (OpenBLAS, all cores), then masked row sum (identical to GPU M2)
//
// The graph is generated by the same integer hash as in trianglebench, so G(n, p, seed) and its triangle
// count are bit-identical to the GPU runs: the CPU result is a cross-check of the GPU result and vice versa.
// Telemetry (every 100 ms): CPU package and DRAM energy from RAPL (x86, needs read access to
// /sys/class/powercap, usually root), CPU temperature (hwmon), median core clock, thermal throttle events.
//
// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT  -  https://github.com/skbotoc1-web/cuda-tensor-bench
